---
import Guide from './Guide.astro';
import '../styles/mechanism.css';
const steps = [
  { name:'Save', title:'A person gives the answer.', text:'A moderator chooses a useful reply. Only that approved knowledge goes into the backpack.', tech:'MongoDB · approved memory', file:'src/memory/learner.ts' },
  { name:'Question', title:'Someone asks it differently.', text:'The forum title, post and replies arrive together. They belong to one conversation.', tech:'Discord · event router', file:'src/bot/handlers/router.ts' },
  { name:'Find', title:'Find the useful facts.', text:'Search this server’s saved knowledge. An exact match first, then words and local embeddings.', tech:'MongoDB · scoped retrieval', file:'src/memory/retriever.ts' },
  { name:'Write', title:'New wording. Same facts.', text:'Paper Instruments or Ollama writes a short answer for this question, using the retrieved evidence.', tech:'Paper Instruments / Ollama', file:'src/agent/orchestrator.ts' },
  { name:'Check', title:'Check the source first.', text:'The response policy checks the citations and links. A draft needs usable evidence before it can go back.', tech:'Response policy · source checks', file:'src/agent/policy.ts' },
  { name:'Reply', title:'Back to the conversation.', text:'A short reply, a link to the original answer, and context for the next follow-up.', tech:'Discord · sourced reply', file:'src/bot/handlers/router.ts' },
];
---
<section class="mechanism-section wrap" id="inside" aria-labelledby="inside-title">
  <div class="mechanism-opening" data-reveal><h2 id="inside-title">How a reply happens.</h2><p>Follow the answer. <br />Everything starts with a person.</p></div>
  <div class="mechanism" data-mechanism data-phase="0" data-route="answer">
    <div class="mechanism-top"><div class="mechanism-routes" role="group" aria-label="Choose a question"><button type="button" data-mechanism-route="answer" aria-pressed="true">Known question</button><button type="button" data-mechanism-route="quiet" aria-pressed="false">New question</button></div><button class="mechanism-play" type="button" data-mechanism-play aria-label="Pause explanation" hidden><svg viewBox="0 0 20 20" width="18" height="18" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true"><path class="pause-glyph" d="M5 4h3v12H5zm7 0h3v12h-3z"/><path class="play-glyph" d="m6 3 11 7-11 7z"/></svg><span data-play-label>Pause</span></button></div>
    <div class="mechanism-caption"><h3 data-mechanism-title>{steps[0].title}</h3><p data-mechanism-copy>{steps[0].text}</p></div>
    <div class="mechanism-theatre" data-mechanism-theatre aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="mechanism-memory" data-object="memory"><div class="memory-pages"><span></span><span></span><span></span></div><span class="object-name">Saved knowledge</span></div>
      <div class="mechanism-guide" data-object="guide"><Guide pose="save" /><span class="guide-ground"></span></div>
      <div class="evidence-sheet" data-object="evidence"><div class="sheet-author"><span class="person-dot">S</span><span>Sam · moderator</span><svg viewBox="0 0 20 20" width="20" height="20" fill="none"><path d="m4 10 4 4 8-8" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></div><p>Keep the same repo.<br />Push fixes before close.</p><span class="sheet-source">Original answer</span></div>
      <div class="question-sheet" data-object="question"><span class="sheet-author"><span class="person-dot person-dot--nia">N</span>Nia · new post</span><p data-visual-question>New fix. New link?</p></div>
      <div class="retrieval-facts" data-object="facts"><span class="fact-note fact-note--one">Same repo</span><span class="fact-note fact-note--two">Before close</span><span class="fact-note fact-note--three">Add a changelog</span></div>
      <div class="model-pass" data-object="model"><span class="model-knot"><svg viewBox="0 0 80 80" fill="none"><path d="M40 9c17 0 31 14 31 31S57 71 40 71 9 57 9 40 23 9 40 9Z" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3"/><path d="M40 9c-19 12-19 50 0 62M40 9c19 12 19 50 0 62M9 40h62" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3"/></svg></span><span data-model-caption>Question + evidence</span></div>
      <div class="reply-sheet" data-object="reply"><div class="sheet-author"><img src="/brand/guide.svg" width="28" height="28" alt=""/><span>ThreadSherpa</span></div><p>Keep your link. Push the fix before submissions close.</p><span class="reply-source"><svg viewBox="0 0 20 20" width="17" height="17" fill="none"><path d="m8 12 4-4m-5 2-2 2a3 3 0 0 0 4 4l3-3m1-3 2-2a3 3 0 0 0-4-4L8 7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg>Sam’s original answer</span></div>
      <div class="policy-check" data-object="check"><svg viewBox="0 0 64 64" fill="none"><path d="m32 5 23 9v18c0 12-12 23-23 27C21 55 9 44 9 32V14z" fill="currentColor"/><path d="m22 32 7 7 14-15" stroke="#100f15" stroke-width="4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg><span>Source checked</span></div>
      <div class="quiet-result" data-object="quiet"><span class="quiet-hand"><svg viewBox="0 0 56 56" fill="none"><path d="M14 30V13a4 4 0 0 1 8 0v13-17a4 4 0 0 1 8 0v17-15a4 4 0 0 1 8 0v17-10a4 4 0 0 1 8 0v17c0 13-8 18-17 18-7 0-11-4-15-9L5 30a4 4 0 0 1 6-5l3 5Z" fill="currentColor"/></svg></span><p data-quiet-caption>No saved facts for this.</p><span>No bot reply</span></div>
      <div class="transport-note" data-object="transport"><svg viewBox="0 0 34 42" width="34" height="42" fill="none"><rect x="2" y="2" width="30" height="38" rx="5" fill="currentColor"/><path d="M10 13h14M10 21h10M10 29h14" stroke="#100f15" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg></div>
      <div class="flow-trail" data-object="trail"><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="mechanism-foot"><div class="mechanism-tech"><span data-mechanism-tech>{steps[0].tech}</span><a data-mechanism-source href={`https://github.com/sea-deep/threadsherpa/blob/main/${steps[0].file}`} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><code data-mechanism-file>{steps[0].file}</code><img src="/icons/arrow-right-up-linear.svg" width="16" height="16" alt=""/></a></div><button type="button" class="mechanism-replay" data-mechanism-replay hidden><svg viewBox="0 0 20 20" width="18" height="18" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 7a7 7 0 1 1-1 6M4 2v5h5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>Replay</button></div>
    <div class="mechanism-chapters" aria-label="Explanation steps">{steps.map((item,index)=><button type="button" data-mechanism-step={index} aria-current={index===0?'step':undefined}><span>{item.name}</span><span class="chapter-fill" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>)}</div>
    <ol class="mechanism-transcript">{steps.map(item=><li><strong>{item.title}</strong> {item.text}</li>)}<li>If no useful evidence is found, skip generation. Keep the thread quiet and queue it for a moderator.</li></ol>
  </div>
  <details class="mechanism-details"><summary>Read the implementation details <span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><div class="implementation-grid"><div><h3>Memory has boundaries.</h3><p>Only a moderator’s save becomes approved knowledge. The saved entry keeps its question, source and scope. Repeated saves reuse the existing knowledge.</p><p>Retrieval stays inside the server. Optional web sources must be chosen by a moderator.</p></div><div><h3>One bounded pass.</h3><p>The model gets the question, thread context and retrieved facts. It writes one to three sentences. The original reply is evidence, not a template.</p><p>Citation and link checks establish the source. People still judge whether the advice is right. No usable evidence means no generation call.</p></div></div></details>
  <script type="application/json" data-mechanism-data set:html={JSON.stringify(steps)} />
  <script>import '../scripts/mechanism';</script>
</section>
